  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Make People Stronger - vervolg</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Proper morgue facilities are not widely available in Uganda. Burials are however considered culturally highly important &#x2013; families spend an average of &#x20ac;2000-5000 on a typical burial. Due to climatic circumstances, there is a time constraint to burials, even though the more affluent members of a given family tend to live abroad. Extending the time between the actual death and burial increases the chance for the expatriate family member to be able to attend the funeral. This is a market that is currently under-serviced, despite the clear demand. Dutch Social Enterprise Make People Stronger (MPS) wants to service this market by opening several cooled morgue facilities across the country that will enable respectful and hygienic burial services and extended time between death and burial ceremonies. Furthermore, through its business model, MPS wants to use its profits to support local hospitals and charitable organisations. This DGGF TA is to support the build of the first morgue in Uganda. The morgue will be shipped from the Netherlands and will then be build on the grounds of a partnering hospital.</narrative>
  </description>
